From a204f69f3f52842391fb465889cab82102b425fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wdstudiosma <mikaelamanfo@wdstudios.tech>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:34:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Meshlets): cluster-DAG LOD, two-pass occlusion, geometry
 streaming/paging

The full continuation of the hardware mesh-shader program, on top of the
Phase 5 AS cluster cull:

- Fix: shader hot-reload assert (BuildShaderAndRenderData deferred pipeline
  state to FrameBeginInternal) and AS-cull constants lost on packet-rebuild
  frames (RHI drops a same-frame SRG recompile; creation now writes live
  constants).
- AS-cull pass parity: shared cluster-cull AS (MeshletsCullAS.azsli) with
  culled depth/motion/shadow PSOs; shadow runs the AS in cut-only mode so
  shadow geometry matches the shaded cut. Freeze-cull works on the AS path.
- HiZ occlusion: persistent double-buffered pyramid (GpuCullAndDrawPass now
  uses HiZGeneratePersistentTemplate + exposes HiZOutput), prev-frame
  pyramid bound via the cull barrier pass, per-cluster + big-triangle tests.
- Two-pass occlusion: pass 1 records dispatched clusters in a frame-id
  ledger (no clear pass), the injected MeshletsLateDepthPass re-tests only
  skipped clusters against THIS frame's pyramid; forward/motion cull against
  the current pyramid. Occlusion-safe depth prevents pyramid feedback.
- Phase 6 cluster-DAG LOD (pack v3): builder DAG via meshopt partition +
  simplifyWithAttributes (LOCK_BORDER|SPARSE|ERROR_ABSOLUTE), group-shared
  monotonic errors, leaf-first layout; flat per-cluster cut test in both
  cull paths; DAG-depth debug coloring; per-instance LOD ladder bypassed.
- Phase 7 streaming (pack v4): self-contained leaf pages + always-resident
  interior pages, ParentIndex group mapping, CPU residency core (classifier,
  hysteresis band, LRU-under-pressure, reserved slots, churn/starved
  stats), global fixed-slot page pool uploaded by a compute dispatch on the
  cull pass, residency-aware fail-safe-coarse cut, paged fetch in all
  AS-culled mesh shaders, live budget re-sizing, soak simulations, and the
  r_meshletsStreamingExclusive monolithic-drop switch (the VRAM reclaim).
- Unit tests: DAG invariants, page self-containment, residency behavior,
  streaming soak (budget sweep / teleport / thrash / accounting).

Everything is gated off by default (r_meshletsMsCullAS, r_meshletsDagLod,
r_meshletsTwoPassOcclusion, r_meshletsStreaming*, sidecar opt-ins); v2/v3
packs and every existing path are behavior-identical with the toggles off.

Signed-off-by: wdstudiosma <mikaelamanfo@wdstudios.tech>
